OUTPUT TEXT: "a-fatbin** (fatbinary embedded in the Rust binary). **No CUTLASS, no Triton, no PyTorch, Python, or C++ in the final binary.** |\n| Kernel compilation | **`nvcc`** (AOT, `-arch=sm_120a` for SASS, `-gencode arch=compute_120f,code=sm_122` for FP4-fast grouped research path; CUDA 13.1 for main, CUDA 12.8 for MMQ/GGUF path) |\n| Kernel launch | **`cudarc`** `launch_kernel` (driver API, zero-copy args, no Python dispatch) | launches |\n| HTTP server | **`axum` + `tokio`** (OpenAI-compatible `/v1/chat/completions`, streaming SSE) |\n| Model format | **GGUF** (primary), **Safetensors** (secondary, for MoE research) |\n| Quantization formats | **W4A16 (Marlin), W8A8 (Marlin), W4A16 (MMQ), FP8 (block-scale), FP4 (block-scale)** |\n\n### Why Rust + raw `.cu` over alternatives\n\n| Alternative | Why rejected |\n|---|--- runtimes |\n| Python (vLLM/SGLang) | Structural tax: per-step Python dispatch + GC + mandatory CUDA graphs (8× penalty without graphs on sm_120 per vLL vLLM #37252) + no host expert offload (OOM on >24 GB MoE). |\n| C++ (llama.cpp) | Per-op dispatch overhead, no native async I/O, re-copies hot experts every token, MMQ segfaults under CUDA 13.1 on sm_120. |\n| CUTLASS | TMA-warp-specialized grouped tactics fail to initialize on sm_120; CUTLASS is a research library, not a shipping kernel library for consumer Blackwell. |\n| Triton | No sm_120 support yet; no block-scale FP4/FP8; no MoE grouped GEMM. |\n| PyTorch | Structural tax (Python dispatch, GC, CUDA graphs), no host expert offload, OOM on >24 GB MoE. |\n\n### Why raw `."
